                <pb facs="0447" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg313"/>

                <head>No. 215.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 15,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 329.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I desire to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 639 of the 5th of May last, and to express the Department’s satisfaction
                    that the intricate question relating to the etiquette to be observed between the
                    Chinese foreign office and the diplomatic body at Peking on New Year’s Day has
                    at last been disposed of.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
